WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.030
- I'm here with Cecily Strong!

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:05.340
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:06.560
And that cute dress or shirt.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:08.117
I don't know what it is but it's cute.

00:00:08.117 --> 00:00:10.470
My next guest is one of the best dancers

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:11.780
this side of the Mississippi, y'all.

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:15.010
She is an Emmy and two-time
Mirrorball Trophy winner.

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.680
You can see her each week doing her thing

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.442
on "Dancing With the Stars" on ABC.

00:00:18.442 --> 00:00:20.690
Give it up for Cheryl Burke!

00:00:20.690 --> 00:00:23.273
(upbeat music)

00:00:26.203 --> 00:00:30.073
(audience cheers and applauds)

00:00:30.073 --> 00:00:31.573
- I can't hug you!

00:00:33.607 --> 00:00:35.660
So, hello, I love your
outfit first of all.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:36.570
And have you met Cecily before?

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:38.102
- No, hi! Nice to meet you.

00:00:38.102 --> 00:00:40.031
- Hi! Nice to meet you,

00:00:40.031 --> 00:00:41.350
- [Cheryl] This is so
crazy. This is great.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:42.590
- This way.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:43.427
- I know, it's weird, they're all live.

00:00:43.427 --> 00:00:44.650
- It's so crazy.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:46.460
- I just, I've had a couple
friends on the show this season.

00:00:46.460 --> 00:00:47.640
They're like, wait, are those, like, real,

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.473
or are they video?

00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:49.466
- [Cheryl] Yeah, right?

00:00:49.466 --> 00:00:50.299
- Like, is it just tape?

00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:51.132
And I'm like nope, they're real.

00:00:51.132 --> 00:00:52.600
- On "Dancing With the
Stars" I wish we had this.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:53.501
- [Kelly] No, it's really cool.

00:00:53.501 --> 00:00:54.334
- This is great.

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:55.240
- It's very helpful,
like, just with laughing,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:56.720
and, like, you know, real clapping.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:57.783
- Exactly, exactly.

00:00:59.012 --> 00:01:01.817
- So, okay, so, well, congrats
on your 23rd season on

00:01:01.817 --> 00:01:02.800
"Dancing With the Stars."

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.430
Has it been challenging with COVID?

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:05.560
Everybody's kind of navigating that.

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:07.270
- It is. It is, 'cause,
you know, we're dancers,

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:09.350
so we're very touchy
feely, you know, so, like,

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.220
just to pass people on
set and just do, like,

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:14.180
a social distancing
hug, hi, is really hard.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:16.720
But they've been doing great
because, you know, for us,

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.240
now, we feel safe on set,

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:19.480
and I think that's very important.

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:20.313
- Yeah.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.520
- But they do keep us just
to our dance partners.

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.810
We get tested every day
except for weekends,

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:26.890
and, like, today, I took
my third COVID test,

00:01:26.890 --> 00:01:27.850
so we're good.

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:29.270
I'm negative three times, so we're good.

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:30.103
- I'm telling you.

00:01:30.103 --> 00:01:32.150
I have this conversation
with Carson from "The Voice"

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:32.983
all the time.

00:01:32.983 --> 00:01:34.330
I don't know how often
y'all are tested, Cecily,

00:01:34.330 --> 00:01:39.330
but we are tested so much,
like, I am a COVID free zone.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:40.850
- Exactly, yeah.

00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.530
- It's insane, 'cause nobody
will take anybody else's test.

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.363
- [Cheryl] Right.

00:01:44.363 --> 00:01:45.536
- You have to do them for all
the individual, it's crazy.

00:01:45.536 --> 00:01:46.369
- [Cheryl] Yes.

00:01:46.369 --> 00:01:47.940
- But we're all safe, so it's good.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.640
Well, you're partnered with
a Backstreet Boy, AJ McLean,

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:53.290
so, did you have his poster
on your wall growing up?

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:54.123
Were you a fan?

00:01:54.123 --> 00:01:56.940
- So, NSYNC was my...

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.060
Sorry, AJ, but he knows this already.

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.820
I loved NSYNC 'cause of the dancing.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.653
- [Kelly] Yes.

00:02:01.653 --> 00:02:04.730
- But I loved Backstreet Boys'
music, so I think, you know,

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:05.563
it was half and half

00:02:05.563 --> 00:02:08.420
But I also had, like, Luke Perry's poster.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:09.420
- [Kelly] Oh my God.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:12.140
- New Kids on the Block,
Bedsheets, you name it.

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.530
- Oh, my sister had all of that.

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.340
Oh my gosh, like, buttons and towels.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:16.383
- [Cheryl] Yes, everything.

00:02:16.383 --> 00:02:17.520
- I was like, it's a lot, Alyssa.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.015
Yeah. Were you into boy bands, Cecily?

00:02:21.015 --> 00:02:23.820
- I, my only two pictures...

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:27.803
I had, like, my posters
were Broadway shows.

00:02:27.803 --> 00:02:28.636
- I love you.

00:02:28.636 --> 00:02:33.000
- And then I was like, oh, I
should have a boy on the wall.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.640
And so I cut out these
two tiny pictures from

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:40.500
Seventeen Magazine of Leonardo
DiCaprio and Brad Renfro.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.333
- That's awesome.

00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:43.991
- Right, and I was like,
they are real actors.

00:02:43.991 --> 00:02:45.470
- Real actors.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:47.290
I was such a messed up kid, man, I mean,

00:02:47.290 --> 00:02:48.840
'cause I feel like you're
too young to have, like,

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.810
Steven Tyler on your wall
when you're a little girl,

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:52.240
like, it's a little weird.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.390
Like, you definitely know
the girl has daddy issues

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.870
if you're walking into her room

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.901
and there's Steven Tyler on the wall.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:02:58.878
But I love him.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:00.500
- Alicia Silverstone, that
music video. I was obsessed.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:01.430
- Oh my God, "Jaded."

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:03.170
No, that wasn't "Jaded." That was -

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:04.360
- [Cheryl] It was -
- "Crazy"?

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:05.862
- Yes, "Crazy."

00:03:05.862 --> 00:03:06.695
- [Kelly] Or maybe, yeah,
that was good, yeah.

00:03:06.695 --> 00:03:07.528
- [Cecily] Or, "Crying."

00:03:07.528 --> 00:03:08.361
- Or "Crying," yes.

00:03:08.361 --> 00:03:09.701
- "Crying," "Crying."

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:10.534
- Isn't it weird to imagine, like, you,

00:03:10.534 --> 00:03:12.550
like doing your dad's friend's video?

00:03:12.550 --> 00:03:16.050
'Cause they were really close.

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:17.718
Like, Liv and -

00:03:17.718 --> 00:03:19.210
- That was, yeah, Liv and...

00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:21.070
Yeah, yeah, yeah. I love that one.

00:03:21.070 --> 00:03:23.510
Okay, so, Cheryl, who
sustained more injuries,

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.320
I'm just curious, over the
years, you or your partners?

00:03:26.320 --> 00:03:28.290
- Well, I've had 22 partners

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:29.990
'cause I danced with
Emmitt Smith twice, so -

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:32.260
- I thought you were gonna
say I've had 22 injuries.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.093
- Oh, I hope not.

00:03:33.093 --> 00:03:35.100
- I was like, oh my
God, never be a dancer.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:35.933
This is the PSA.

00:03:35.933 --> 00:03:37.710
- But it's never been, not so much me,

00:03:37.710 --> 00:03:39.420
more like, I've been injuring my partners.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:40.870
Just 'cause it's the, first of all,

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.830
the schedule is just really crazy.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:46.320
So, we have seven days a week
for about 3 1/2 months, right?

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:47.760
And we're just pounding our bodies.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:49.630
And especially for the
celebrities that come on the show,

00:03:49.630 --> 00:03:50.900
they're not used to doing this.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:51.733
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:03:51.733 --> 00:03:54.320
- They're moving body parts
that they've never moved before.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.670
Even, so, athletes get injured.

00:03:55.670 --> 00:03:57.243
I injured... I wouldn't say I.

00:03:57.243 --> 00:03:58.900
I wouldn't take full responsibility,

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.880
but I am definitely taking some.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.870
Ray Lewis was my partner last season.

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.203
First football player to ever get injured.

00:04:05.203 --> 00:04:07.110
My fault.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:09.850
Then we had Tom DeLay, I danced with.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.100
Fractured both his feet.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:14.605
Cristian de la Fuente, broke
his arm live on television

00:04:14.605 --> 00:04:16.804
when we did the samba, and
the very end we had this dip.

00:04:16.804 --> 00:04:18.396
And then all of a sudden I feel my head

00:04:18.396 --> 00:04:19.734
just crash to the dance floor.

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:22.400
And then Tom Bergeron at the
time had to cut to commercial

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:23.747
'cause he broke his arm.

00:04:23.747 --> 00:04:27.490
- I don't think that
you're the best person

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.846
to promote yourself as a dance partner.

00:04:28.846 --> 00:04:29.731
- No, probably not.

00:04:29.731 --> 00:04:30.840
But you know, it's okay, it's all right.

00:04:30.840 --> 00:04:32.460
I'm just saying, caution.

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:33.293
- Yeah.

00:04:33.293 --> 00:04:34.420
No, that's a lot of work.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:36.070
I've only gone on there and sang.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:37.175
- Yes, yes, I remember.

00:04:37.175 --> 00:04:38.008
- And like, watching everyone, I'm like,

00:04:38.008 --> 00:04:40.004
oh my God, this is a lot of
work for these people to do.

00:04:40.004 --> 00:04:40.930
- Well, we used to pass each other a lot.

00:04:40.930 --> 00:04:42.140
Like, when you did "Idol."

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:42.973
- [Kelly] Yes!

00:04:42.973 --> 00:04:44.390
- So, I started back in season two, 2006.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:45.223
- [Kelly] Wow!

00:04:45.223 --> 00:04:46.590
- So, I remember you guys.

00:04:46.590 --> 00:04:48.200
- I came every season, yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.850
Well, okay, so you also
designed a face mask.

00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:51.683
- [Cheryl] Yes.

00:04:51.683 --> 00:04:53.033
- That you can wear while you dance.

00:04:53.033 --> 00:04:53.866
- Yes, yeah.

00:04:53.866 --> 00:04:54.699
- [Kelly] So, that's pretty cool.

00:04:54.699 --> 00:04:55.532
So, is it, like, ventilated or something,

00:04:55.532 --> 00:04:56.365
'cause it's gotta be so hot.

00:04:56.365 --> 00:04:58.080
- No, it's actually, so, I wanted,

00:04:58.080 --> 00:05:00.930
I had this thing going on
way before the pandemic.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:02.730
I did a live stage show in Japan,

00:05:02.730 --> 00:05:05.270
and I saw all these beautiful
Japanese women and men

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:06.530
wearing, like, designer clothes,

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:08.040
but then they had a dental face mask.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.850
And I was like, went up to
my agent, and I was like,

00:05:09.850 --> 00:05:11.480
we gotta come out with face masks.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:12.600
And she was like, you're crazy.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:13.433
And then, a series of -

00:05:13.433 --> 00:05:14.845
- [Kelly] Oh, who's laughing now.

00:05:14.845 --> 00:05:16.110
- [Cheryl] Exactly.

00:05:16.110 --> 00:05:18.090
A series of unfortunate
events, obviously, happened,

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.050
and I was like, okay,
now's the time to do it.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:22.270
And I don't know about you,
but when I would wear masks,

00:05:22.270 --> 00:05:23.910
I would be swallowing my mask.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:25.177
Like, you'd be laughing,
crying, you're swallowing it.

00:05:25.177 --> 00:05:26.380
- [Kelly] Oh, it sucks it in.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.320
- It sucks it in, right?

00:05:27.320 --> 00:05:29.067
And so, I was like,
there's gotta be a way of

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:31.850
creating something that
you can actually breathe in

00:05:31.850 --> 00:05:33.326
while still being CDC approved,

00:05:33.326 --> 00:05:35.300
and that's what happened.

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.160
So, and then I just said,
why not add some glitter?

00:05:37.160 --> 00:05:37.993
'Cause I love glitter. Who doesn't?

00:05:37.993 --> 00:05:40.620
- And I wanted that glitter. I love you.

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:43.683
Well, you can see "Dancing
With the Stars" Mondays on ABC.

